    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"just disappearing\" pattern across multiple product lines points to a few possibilities: **mis-scans** (an operator scans RES-992-X but the WMS deducts a component that's actually sitting in a nearby bin), **sample/QA pulls that were taken but never returned or logged**, and honestly, **theft** — small, high-value electronic parts like CPUs and memory are frequent pilferage targets because they're easy to conceal.\n\nA subtle one worth ruling out: check whether physical bins have **residual stock not registered in the WMS** (parts that fell behind shelving, stuck in tote corners, or left in return carts). Since your variance is consistently negative but small, a Marie Kondo-style deep clean of the pick faces might literally find your missing parts. I'd reorder your investigation priorities as: process audit first, then the physical sweep, then theft investigation — ruling out innocent explanations before suspecting people.",
